From 6e6f3e5b10d41d871448e7a9bbfeebc4f27829d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pucawo <github@pucawo.de>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 00:12:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] docs(phase-2): correct stash-pop ref in deploy runbook
 (codex F6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`git stash pop "phase-2-deploy-stash"` is invalid — git stash takes a
stash@{N} reference, not a free-form message. Following the runbook
literally would silently fail to restore the production customizations
saved at the start of Stage 2.

Replace with a small `git stash list | grep | cut` lookup that resolves
the message back to the stash@{N} ref, plus an inline note explaining
why the message-as-ref form does not work.
---
 deployment/phase-2-deploy-runbook.md | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/deployment/phase-2-deploy-runbook.md b/deployment/phase-2-deploy-runbook.md
index a7c539e..e2224b7 100644
--- a/deployment/phase-2-deploy-runbook.md
+++ b/deployment/phase-2-deploy-runbook.md
@@ -74,8 +74,16 @@ gesehen):
 4. `api/server/routes/files/index.js` — append-only, sauber.
 
 ```bash
-# Nach erfolgreichem Apply:
-git stash pop "phase-2-deploy-stash"   # bestehende customizations zurück
+# Nach erfolgreichem Apply: Stash wieder zurückholen.
+# WICHTIG: `git stash pop "phase-2-deploy-stash"` ist KEIN gültiger Stash-Ref —
+# git stash erwartet stash@{N}. Über die Message muss erst der Index gefunden
+# werden, oder direkt `stash@{0}` wenn nichts dazwischen gestashed wurde.
+STASH_REF=$(git stash list | grep "phase-2-deploy-stash" | head -1 | cut -d: -f1)
+if [ -n "$STASH_REF" ]; then
+  git stash pop "$STASH_REF"
+else
+  echo "phase-2-deploy-stash nicht gefunden — git stash list manuell prüfen."
+fi
 # → ggf. nochmal mergen falls Konflikte
 ```
 
